        "quote": "Compound of 玄(くろ) (kuro, “deep, profound”) + 人(うと) (-uto, “person”)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "The term 人 (hito, “person”) appears in various older compounds with a root form of 人 (*puto → *buto → *udo, *puto → *futo → *uto). This form is never seen in isolation, and it often undergoes further phonetic changes to combine with preceding vowels. Compare the formation of 仲人 (nakōdo), from naka + udo; 旅人 (tabiudo), from tabi + udo; 素人 (shirōto), from shiro + uto."
      }
